' ======================================================================
' L0 — bottom of the graph. Depends on NO internal crate.
' ======================================================================

package "L0  rs-matter-utils  (no internal deps)" #FEF2F2 {

  class Error {
    - code : ErrorCode
    - backtrace   <<cfg std+backtrace>>
    - inner       <<cfg alloc+backtrace>>
    --
    + code() : ErrorCode
    --
    embedded: == ErrorCode == **1 byte**
  }

  enum ErrorCode {
    **79 variants, flat**
    ..
    == status-like (~22, re-verify) ==
    ConstraintError, NotFound
    InvalidInState, InvalidCommand
    ResourceExhausted, Busy, Failure
    AttributeNotFound, CommandNotFound
    ...
    ..
    == internal faults (~56) ==
    NoSpace / NoSpaceExchanges
      / NoSpaceSessions
    InvalidState
    Utf8Fail, RwLock, StdIoError
    BtpError, MdnsError, DBusError
    ...
  }

  Error *-- ErrorCode
}

note right of ErrorCode
  **THE BINDING CONSTRAINT**
  This crate is the bottom of the graph, so
  ErrorCode cannot name a type from any crate
  above it.

  => ErrorCode::Status(IMStatusCode) -- the
  design agreed before the split -- is **not
  implementable here**. It is a Cargo cycle,
  which no Box or indirection fixes.

  Open: move IMStatusCode down, or add a new
  L0 crate (rs-matter-error) holding Error,
  ErrorCode and IMStatusCode together, since
  they are mutually referential by design.
end note

' ======================================================================
' L1 — im-core
' ======================================================================

package "L1  rs-matter-im-core  (<- utils, tlv)" #EFF6FF {

  enum IMStatusCode <<spec>> {
    Success = 0, Failure = 1
    0x7D .. 0xD1
    34 values
    --
    + to_error_code() : Option<ErrorCode>
  }

  class Status <<spec: StatusIB>> {
    + status : IMStatusCode
    + cluster_status : **Option<NonZeroU8>**
    ..
    narrowed from Option<u16> -- **DONE**
    6 bytes -> 2 bytes
  }

  class CmdStatus   <<spec>> {
    + path
    status
    command_ref
  }
  class AttrStatus  <<spec>> {
    + path
    status
  }
  class EventStatus <<spec>> {
    + path
    status
  }

  Status *-- IMStatusCode
  CmdStatus   *-- Status
  AttrStatus  *-- Status
  EventStatus *-- Status
}

ErrorCode -[#B91C1C]-> IMStatusCode : **From** — maps the status-like\nvariants, **collapses the rest**\nto Failure (_ => Failure)
IMStatusCode ..> ErrorCode : to_error_code()\nNone for Success

note bottom of IMStatusCode
  Both conversions live HERE, in im-core --
  the only legal direction. im-core may name
  ErrorCode (below it); utils may never name
  IMStatusCode.

  The duplication these reconcile IS the
  defect: ~22 ErrorCode variants restate
  values that already exist in this enum.
end note

' ======================================================================
' L2 — dm-core: the staging channel
' ======================================================================

package "L2  rs-matter-dm-core  (<- utils, tlv, crypto, im-core)" #ECFDF5 {

  class CmdDetails {
    + cluster_status : **Cell<Option<NonZeroU8>>**
    --
    + set_cluster_status(Option<NonZeroU8>)
    + cluster_status() : Option<NonZeroU8>
    + status(IMStatusCode) : Option<CmdStatus>
  }
  class AttrDetails {
    + cluster_status : **Cell<Option<NonZeroU8>>**
    --
    same shape, builds AttrStatus
  }

  interface InvokeContext {
    + cmd()  : &CmdDetails
  }
  interface WriteContext  {
    + attr() : &AttrDetails
  }
  interface ReadContext   {
    + attr() : &AttrDetails
  }

  InvokeContext ..> CmdDetails
  WriteContext  ..> AttrDetails
  ReadContext   ..> AttrDetails
}

CmdDetails  ..> CmdStatus  : status()
AttrDetails ..> AttrStatus : status()

note bottom of CmdDetails
  **The staging channel — deliberate.**
  The cluster byte travels HERE, beside the
  Result, not inside Error. Costs 0 bytes on
  every Result<(),Error> in the workspace.

  Hook traits receive NO context, so a hook
  cannot reach set_cluster_status itself.
  Bridging that is what the planned
  ClusterStatus / stage() pattern is for.
end note

